## Hooks: Correct Usage

### 7. Include All Dependencies

**Problem:** Missing dependencies cause stale data or infinite loops.

```typescript
// BAD - missing dependency
useEffect(() => {
    fetchData(organizationId);
}, []); // organizationId changes won't trigger refetch

// BAD - missing callback dependency
const handleSave = useCallback(() => {
    saveItem(itemId);
}, []); // itemId changes won't be reflected
```

```typescript
// GOOD
useEffect(() => {
    if (!organizationId) return;
    fetchData(organizationId);
}, [organizationId]);

const handleSave = useCallback(() => {
    saveItem(itemId);
}, [itemId]);
```

### 8. Use useRefFor for Stable Callbacks

**Problem:** Callbacks need access to current values but shouldn't re-create on every change.

```typescript
// BAD - callback recreated when someValue changes
const handleClick = useCallback(() => {
    doSomething(someValue);
}, [someValue]); // changes often, causing re-renders

// BAD - stale closure
const handleClick = useCallback(() => {
    doSomething(someValue); // someValue is stale!
}, []);
```

```typescript
// GOOD - stable callback with current value
import useRefFor from "@/submodules/react-components/hooks/useRefFor";

const someValueRef = useRefFor(someValue);

const handleClick = useCallback(() => {
    doSomething(someValueRef.current); // always current
}, []); // stable reference
```

### 9. i18n: Depend on Language, Not t Function

**Problem:** The `t` function reference changes, causing unnecessary recalculations.

```typescript
// BAD
const { t } = useTranslation();
const label = useMemo(() => t('myKey'), [t]); // t changes often
```

```typescript
// GOOD
const { t, i18n } = useTranslation();
const label = useMemo(() => t('myKey'), [i18n.language]);
```

