## State Management

### 10. Don't Duplicate Props into State

**Problem:** Syncing prop to state causes bugs and extra renders.

```typescript
// BAD - unnecessary state duplication
function Modal({ isOpen }) {
    const [open, setOpen] = useState(isOpen);
    useEffect(() => setOpen(isOpen), [isOpen]); // sync issues!
    ...
}
```

```typescript
// GOOD - use prop directly
function Modal({ isOpen, onClose }) {
    // Use isOpen directly from props
    if (!isOpen) return null;
    ...
}

// GOOD - controlled component pattern
function Modal({ open, setOpen }) {
    // Parent controls state
    ...
}
```

### 11. Use Redux for Shared State

**Problem:** Prop drilling through many components.

```typescript
// BAD - drilling through many levels
<Parent value={value} setValue={setValue}>
    <Child value={value} setValue={setValue}>
        <GrandChild value={value} setValue={setValue}>
```

```typescript
// GOOD - Redux for shared state
const value = useSelector(selectValue);
const dispatch = useDispatch();
const handleChange = useCallback(() => {
    dispatch(setValue(newValue));
}, [dispatch, newValue]);
```

### 12. Don't Duplicate API Calls

**Problem:** Multiple components fetch the same data independently.

```typescript
// BAD - each component fetches
// ComponentA.tsx
useEffect(() => { fetchEnvVars().then(setVars); }, []);
// ComponentB.tsx  
useEffect(() => { fetchEnvVars().then(setVars); }, []);
```

```typescript
// GOOD - fetch once, share via Redux or props
// Parent or config component fetches once
// Children receive via selector or props
const envVars = useSelector(selectEnvVars);
```

